The data source is a single flat table of ACLED conflict events. Distinct real-world entity types can be grouped as follows. First, the event itself is described by event_id_cnty and event-specific columns; this maps to bsm:Action because event_type values like "Battles" and the event identifier match the notion of a conflict action. Its subject is event_id_cnty with template "acled_event_{event_id_cnty}". Second, actor1 and actor2 are separate actor entities that appear across rows; their names are unique enough to serve as subjects with templates "acled_actor_{actor1}" and "acled_actor_{actor2}". Sample values such as "Military Forces of Poland" indicate organised groups, so they map to bsm:Organisation. Third, the location columns (location, country, admin levels, coordinates) describe a geographic place; we treat location plus country as subject "acled_location_{location}_{country}" mapping to bsm:Location. Fourth, the latitude and longitude pairs describe a point geometry; subject "acled_point_{latitude}_{longitude}" maps to bsm:AbsolutePoint.

For the Event (Action) class, event_date maps to bsm:eventStartDateTime (name match), notes to bsm:actionDescriptionText (description), event_type to bsm:classificationCode (name), source to bsm:sourceIdentifier (name). The event has a geographic location reference to the Location entity (structural, using identical template) and involved actors referencing the Actor entities (name). For Actor1/2, actor name maps to bsm:conceptName (inherited from Concept), assoc_actor_1/2 to bsm:descriptionText (description), inter1/2 to bsm:typeName (name). For Location, location maps to bsm:locationName (name) and hasGeometry references the AbsolutePoint (structural). For AbsolutePoint, latitude/longitude map to bsm:latitudeDecimal and bsm:longitudeDecimal (name). Columns with no fitting ontology term (year, time_precision, disorder_type, sub_event_type, interaction, civilian_targeting, iso, region, admin1-3, geo_precision, source_scale, fatalities, tags, timestamp, population_*) are left unmapped.

